---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getAdjacent } from '../../../data/concepts';

const slug = 'what-is-bittensor';
const { next } = getAdjacent(slug);
---
<BaseLayout
  title="What is Bittensor — Wiki — OpenTAO"
  description="The shape of an open network for machine intelligence — in 800 words."
  section="beginner"
>
  <header class="border-b hairline">
    <div class="article px-6 pt-16 pb-12">
      <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[color:var(--color-fg-dim)] mb-8 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">OpenTAO</a><span>/</span>
        <a href="/beginner/wiki" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">Wiki</a><span>/</span>
        <span>Network basics</span><span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">What is Bittensor</span>
      </div>
      <div class="section-label mb-4">Cluster I · Network basics · concept 01</div>
      <h1 class="font-serif font-medium text-[56px] md:text-[64px] leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.025em]">
        What is <span class="italic">Bittensor</span>?
      </h1>
      <p class="font-serif italic font-normal text-2xl text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] mt-6 leading-[1.4]">
        The shape of an open network for machine intelligence — in 800 words.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-mono text-[color:var(--color-fg-dim)]">
          <span><span class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)]" id="depth-read-time">25</span> min read</span>
          <span class="opacity-30">·</span>
          <span>last verified 2026·05·27 by @editorial</span>
          <span class="opacity-30">·</span>
          <span>3 contributors</span>
        </div>
        <div class="depth-toggle" id="depth-toggle">
          <button data-depth="short">5 min</button>
          <button data-depth="long" class="active">25 min</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="border-b hairline">
    <article class="article px-6 py-16" data-depth="long" id="depth-article">
      <p class="lead">
        Most networks reward one kind of work. Bitcoin rewards hashing; Filecoin rewards storage. Bittensor is built for many kinds of work at once — and the kinds aren't fixed in advance. Anyone with an idea about what "useful intelligence" could mean is welcome to launch a market for it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's the shape of the whole thing: a single chain underneath, and dozens of competing intelligence markets running on top. Today there are <strong>128 of them</strong> live; tomorrow there could be more.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why-it-matters"><span class="index">I.</span>Why it matters</h2>
      <p class="long-only">
        Most AI today is concentrated in a handful of companies. Their models are reachable only through APIs, their training data is private, and the value flows to whoever owns the platform.
      </p>
      <p class="long-only">
        Bittensor inverts this. Anyone can join a subnet as a <a class="inline" href="/beginner/concepts/miner">miner</a> and contribute work; anyone can join as a <a class="inline" href="/beginner/concepts/validator">validator</a> and grade that work; anyone can launch a new subnet for a new kind of intelligence. <span class="term" title="The native token of Bittensor">TAO</span> flows to whoever produces value — not to whoever owns the platform.
      </p>
      <p class="short-only">
        Most AI today concentrates in a few companies — closed models, private data, value flows to whoever owns the platform. Bittensor inverts this: anyone can mine, anyone can validate, anyone can launch a new market. <span class="term" title="The native token of Bittensor">TAO</span> follows the work.
      </p>
      <p class="pullquote">
        Whether this is actually a better system depends on the math of the incentives. But the shape, at least, is what makes Bittensor interesting.
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-it-works"><span class="index">II.</span>How it works</h2>
      <p>Three pieces, in order.</p>

      <p class="short-only">
        <strong>Subtensor</strong> is a Substrate blockchain that keeps the books and pays emissions every ~72 minutes. <strong>Subnets</strong> are the markets that run on top — each one defines what miners submit and how validators score it. <strong>Yuma consensus</strong> takes every validator's weights, multiplies by stake, and produces the final reward distribution. About twenty cycles a day.
      </p>

      <div class="long-only">
        <h3><span class="step-num">i.</span>Subtensor, the chain</h3>
        <p>
          Underneath everything is <code>subtensor</code>, a Substrate-based blockchain. It keeps the books: who has TAO, who's registered to what, what validators are saying about which miners. Every <code>block</code> (~12 seconds) and every <code>tempo</code> (~360 blocks ≈ 72 minutes), it settles accounts and pays out emissions.
        </p>

        <h3><span class="step-num">ii.</span>Subnets, the marketplaces</h3>
        <p>
          On top of the chain run subnets. Each one is, in effect, a market for one kind of intelligence: text generation, image generation, reasoning traces, motor control for a robot arm. Each has its own rules about what miners submit and how validators score it. From the chain's point of view, all subnets look the same — they just produce a vector of weights at every tempo.
        </p>

        <h3><span class="step-num">iii.</span>Yuma consensus, the settlement</h3>
        <p>
          At each tempo, every validator submits weights for every miner. <a class="inline" href="/beginner/concepts/yuma-consensus">Yuma</a> aggregates these weights, weighted by each validator's stake, into a final reward distribution. Miners get paid; validators get paid; subnet owners take a fee. The cycle repeats — about twenty times a day, every day.
        </p>

        <div class="figure">[figure] Chain → 128 subnets → per-tempo weights → Yuma aggregation → emission</div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="in-practice"><span class="index">III.</span>In practice</h2>
      <p>If you want to participate, you'll pick one of three roles:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Miner</strong> — you have a GPU and you want to produce work. Read a <a class="inline" href="/mine/playbooks">mining playbook</a> for the subnet you care about.</li>
        <li><strong>Validator</strong> — you have (or can attract) enough TAO stake and you want to grade. Validators take more work to set up but earn from delegations.</li>
        <li><strong>Subnet owner</strong> — you have a new kind of intelligence you want to incentivize. See <a class="inline" href="/build/hackathon">Build a subnet</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="long-only">
        Most newcomers don't decide which role they want until they've read about all three. That's fine — read on, then come back to this page once you know.
      </p>

      <h2 id="going-deeper" class="long-only"><span class="index">IV.</span>Going deeper</h2>
      <div class="going-deeper-list mt-4 long-only">
        <a href="#"><div><div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium">The Bittensor whitepaper</div><div class="meta">PDF · 2021 · math-heavy but short</div></div><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/community/insights"><div><div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Yuma Consensus, slowly</div><div class="meta">Insight · 22 min · hand-traced walk through one block</div></div><span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        <a href="/community/insights"><div><div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium">Why dTAO changed everything</div><div class="meta">Insight · 14 min · the 2024 economic upgrade in retrospect</div></div><span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        <a href="#"><div><div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium">subtensor source on GitHub</div><div class="meta">Code · the chain itself</div></div><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="related"><span class="index">V.</span>Related concepts</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-6">
        <a href="/beginner/concepts/subtensor" class="related-card">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2"><span class="num text-2xl">04</span><span class="section-label">Network basics</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium mb-1">Subtensor, the chain</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] leading-relaxed">A Substrate-based blockchain that keeps everyone's books.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/beginner/concepts/miner" class="related-card">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2"><span class="num text-2xl">08</span><span class="section-label">Roles</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium mb-1">Miner</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] leading-relaxed">The contributor role. Submits work; earns on rank.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/beginner/concepts/validator" class="related-card">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2"><span class="num text-2xl">09</span><span class="section-label">Roles</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium mb-1">Validator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] leading-relaxed">The scorer role. Submits weights; earns on stake.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/beginner/concepts/yuma-consensus" class="related-card">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2"><span class="num text-2xl">17</span><span class="section-label">Consensus</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] font-medium mb-1">Yuma Consensus</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] leading-relaxed">The aggregation rule. Validator weights × stake → reward.</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <section class="border-b hairline">
    <div class="article px-6 py-10">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 text-xs font-mono text-[color:var(--color-fg-dim)]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-5">
          <a href="#" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">Edit on GitHub</a>
          <a href="#" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-fg)]">Suggest an edit</a>
        </div>
        <span>Verified against chain v2.1.4</span>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-8">
        <div class="border hairline rounded-md p-4 opacity-50">
          <div class="text-xs font-mono text-[color:var(--color-fg-dim)] mb-1">← Previous</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] text-sm">(first concept)</div>
        </div>
        {next && (
          <a href={`/beginner/concepts/${next.slug}`} class="border hairline rounded-md p-4 hover:border-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)] transition block">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-[color:var(--color-fg-dim)] mb-1 text-right">Next →</div>
            <div class="text-[color:var(--color-fg)] text-sm text-right font-medium">{next.title}</div>
          </a>
        )}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 text-center">
        <a href="/beginner/wiki" class="text-sm hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)] text-[color:var(--color-fg-muted)]">← All 26 concepts</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    const article = document.getElementById('depth-article');
    const readTime = document.getElementById('depth-read-time');
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#depth-toggle button[data-depth]').forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const depth = btn.dataset.depth || 'long';
        if (article) article.dataset.depth = depth;
        if (readTime) readTime.textContent = depth === 'short' ? '5' : '25';
        document.querySelectorAll('#depth-toggle button[data-depth]').forEach((b) => b.classList.toggle('active', b === btn));
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
      });
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .article p { color: #1c1c22; line-height: 1.75; margin: 22px 0; font-size: 18px; }
  .article p.lead { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.55; color: #0c0c10; margin: 32px 0 40px; letter-spacing: -0.005em; }
  .article p.lead::first-letter { font-size: 56px; line-height: 0.95; float: left; padding: 6px 12px 0 0; font-weight: 500; color: #b8470b; }
  .article p.pullquote { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.5; color: #0c0c10; border-left: 3px solid #b8470b; padding-left: 22px; margin: 36px 0; }
  .article h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 64px 0 16px; color: #0c0c10; }
  .article h2 .index { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: #b8b8be; letter-spacing: 0.06em; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 14px; font-weight: 400; }
  .article h3 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 22px; margin: 36px 0 8px; color: #0c0c10; }
  .article h3 .step-num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: #b8b8be; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-right: 12px; }
  .article ul { margin: 18px 0; padding-left: 24px; }
  .article li { color: #1c1c22; line-height: 1.75; margin: 8px 0; padding-left: 6px; font-size: 17px; }
  .article li::marker { color: #b8b8be; }
  .article a.inline { color: #0c0c10; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: rgba(184,71,11,0.45); text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  .article a.inline:hover { text-decoration-color: #b8470b; }
  .article code { background: #faf8f4; border: 1px solid rgba(15,15,18,0.09); border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 6px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 14px; }
  .article strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .figure { background: #faf8f4; border: 1px dashed rgba(15,15,18,0.18); padding: 32px; text-align: center; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: #767680; border-radius: 6px; margin: 30px 0; }

  .depth-toggle { display: inline-flex; border: 1px solid rgba(15,15,18,0.14); border-radius: 6px; padding: 2px; }
  .depth-toggle button { padding: 4px 12px; font-size: 12px; color: #4a4a52; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); cursor: pointer; background: transparent; border: 0; }
  .depth-toggle button.active { background: rgba(184,71,11,0.1); color: #b8470b; }

  /* Depth-mode visibility — long shows everything, short hides .long-only and reveals .short-only */
  .article[data-depth="long"] .short-only { display: none; }
  .article[data-depth="short"] .long-only { display: none; }

  .related-card { background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid rgba(15,15,18,0.08); padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 6px; transition: all .15s; display: block; }
  .related-card:hover { border-color: rgba(15,15,18,0.22); background: #fafaf9; }
  .related-card .num { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; color: #b8b8be; }

  .going-deeper-list a { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15,15,18,0.06); transition: color .15s; }
  .going-deeper-list a:hover { color: #b8470b; }
  .going-deeper-list a .meta { color: #767680; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; }
  .going-deeper-list a .arrow { margin-left: auto; color: #b8b8be; }

  .term { border-bottom: 1px dashed rgba(184,71,11,0.5); cursor: help; color: #0c0c10; }
</style>
